R=[]
def record(id,kind,name,category,fact,design,components,states,caution,sources,novelty,related='',priority='P2'):
    R.append(dict(id=id,kind=kind,name=name,category=category,scientific_description=fact,design_instructions=design,component_names=components.split(';') if components else [],states=states.split(';'),scientific_caveat=caution,source_ids=sources.split(';'),novelty=novelty,related_baseline=related,priority=priority,verification='source_checked_schematic',design_status='proposed_not_generated'))
def a(id,name,cat,fact,design,components,states,caution,sources,related): record(id,'new_primitive',name,cat,fact,design,components,states,caution,sources,'new',related)
def p(id,name,cat,fact,design,components,states,caution,sources,related=''): record(id,'reuse_preset',name,cat,fact,design,components,states,caution,sources,'reuse',related)
def c(id,name,cat,fact,design,components,states,caution,sources,related='',priority='P2'): record(id,'composite',name,cat,fact,design,components,states,caution,sources,'roadmap_expansion' if related.startswith('roadmap:') else ('baseline_expansion' if related else 'new'),related,priority)

# Distinct building blocks. These are requests for future work, not generated assets.
a('A001','Ferritin protein cage','Proteins','Ferritin provides a hollow protein shell for iron storage.','Plan an intact sphere and a cutaway of the same shell. Keep the cavity, shell and optional iron-core overlay separately addressable. Use a cage silhouette rather than the open tunnel of a chaperonin; do not prescribe atomic surface detail.','generic globular protein','empty;iron-loaded;cutaway','A schematic shell does not establish a species-specific subunit composition. Resolve an exact structure before showing numbered subunits.','FERR','Closest baseline: ring-shaped protein complex and chaperonin barrel; neither is a closed storage cage.')
a('A002','Fibrinogen monomer','Extracellular matrix','Soluble fibrinogen is cleaved to produce fibrin, which can assemble into fibers.','Use an elongated molecule with a central region and two distal lobes connected by slender arms. Provide removable cleavage-site annotations and end attachment points so copies can later form a fiber. Keep the soluble precursor separate from the assembled network.','fibrin fiber','intact;cleavage annotations;assembly-ready','Flexible regions are not completely resolved in many structures. Avoid treating the drawing as exact molecular geometry.','FIB','Closest baseline: fibrin fiber, which represents the polymer rather than soluble precursor.')
a('A003','Lipopolysaccharide molecule','Microbiology','LPS connects a lipid anchor to carbohydrate regions on Gram-negative bacterial surfaces.','Provide a lipid-anchor module beneath an editable sugar-chain region. Mark membrane insertion and extracellular chain endpoints. Offer schematic short-chain and extended-chain states with strain identity left unset.','phospholipid','short carbohydrate;extended carbohydrate;membrane-anchored','Do not infer a fixed sugar sequence, tail count or universal O-antigen length from a generic LPS symbol.','LPS','Closest baseline: glycocalyx and phospholipid; a single LPS building block has a distinct composite molecular architecture.')
a('A004','IgE Fc domain module','Immunology','IgE Fc contains a C-epsilon-2 domain pair and can adopt a bent configuration distinct from IgG Fc.','Design an Fc-only module with paired domain regions and two Fab attachment anchors. Preserve a bent silhouette and expose the receptor-binding side. Full IgE must later reuse two library Fab fragments with this module.','antibody Fab fragment','unbound schematic;receptor-bound placeholder','The cited structure contains Fc, not complete IgE; it does not establish the bound whole-antibody geometry.','IGEF','Closest baseline: antibody Fc fragment and generic IgG antibody; do not relabel IgG Fc as structurally detailed IgE.')
a('A005','Bacterial porin beta-barrel','Microbiology','Classical porins provide water-filled diffusion paths through the bacterial outer membrane.','Plan a short membrane-spanning barrel with a visible lumen and rim loops. Supply side and axial views with separate lumen and membrane anchors. Assemble oligomers from instances; label the selected porin before giving an oligomer count.','transmembrane protein','side view;axial view;restricted lumen','Porins vary in selectivity and oligomeric organization. Do not turn the archetype into a universal ATP-driven transporter.','PORIN','Closest baseline: ligand-gated ion channel and solute carrier transporter; beta-barrel outer-membrane architecture differs.')
a('A006','Aggrecan proteoglycan monomer','Extracellular matrix','Aggrecan has glycosaminoglycan side chains attached to a protein core.','Plan a flexible core with detachable brush-like side chains and a designated attachment region. Preserve chain/core separation for intact and fragmented states. A cartilage panel must assemble these with existing collagen and cell assets.','collagen fibril','intact;reduced side chains;fragmented','This is an aggrecan archetype, not the architecture of every proteoglycan; no quantitative stiffness follows from chain density in the icon.','AGG','Closest baseline: extracellular matrix mesh and collagen fibril; neither represents a single decorated proteoglycan.')
a('A007','Membrane scaffold protein belt','Structural biology','Engineered scaffold proteins stabilize the edge of a nanodisc lipid bilayer.','Plan a reusable open/closed belt around a circular or elliptical membrane boundary, with lipid-facing inner edge and exposed outer edge. Build the disc from existing lipid bilayer components and this belt rather than baking a membrane protein into it.','lipid bilayer cross-section','open belt;closed belt;side view','Disc dimensions and belt stoichiometry depend on the scaffold construct. No single size is implied.','NANO','Closest baseline: coiled-coil protein and ring-shaped protein complex; a lipid-edge scaffold has a different assembly role.')
a('A008','G-quadruplex topology module','Nucleic acids','Guanine-rich nucleic acid can fold into quadruplex structures.','Plan a strand-followable stack of tetrad placeholders with connecting loops. Retain 5-prime and 3-prime anchors. Use a compact topology view and a simplified small-scale icon; reserve base and ion labels for a specified structure.','single-stranded DNA','folded;unfolded comparison','Loop topology and strand orientation are sequence dependent. A telomere need not be folded into this state.','TELO','Closest baseline: DNA double helix and telomere; neither conveys four-stranded folding.')
a('A009','Four-way DNA junction topology module','Nucleic acids','Holliday junctions connect four DNA arms; their conformation depends on sequence and conditions.','Plan four duplex arms with continuous colored strand paths through the junction. Include an explanatory open layout and a compact stacked arrangement. Crossing strands must remain traceable and must not appear severed.','DNA double helix','open schematic;stacked schematic','Open layout is an explanatory design choice. The cited deposition directly supports a stacked-X conformation, not a universal angle.','HJ','Closest baseline: replication fork has three arms; a four-way junction adds a different topology.')
a('A010','Pericyte with vessel-facing processes','Cells','Pericytes are associated with the outside of capillary endothelium.','Plan an elongated nucleated cell whose processes can follow a vessel exterior. Provide a vessel-contact anchor and process handles. Keep the vessel itself separate and leave marker labels optional.','endothelial cell','isolated;vessel-associated orientation','Shape varies by vascular bed. Positioning outside the endothelial lumen is the verified constraint; process lengths are schematic.','CAP','Closest baseline: smooth muscle cell and fibroblast; the vascular wrapping configuration should remain distinguishable.')
a('A011','Paneth cell with apical granule compartment','Cells','Paneth cells occur at intestinal crypt bases and contain antimicrobial secretory granules.','Plan a crypt-compatible epithelial outline with a distinct granule-rich apical region and basal nucleus. Include explicit apical/basal anchors so the cell can be inserted among existing epithelial cells. Keep granules separate for a secretion scene.','columnar epithelial cell;secretory vesicle','granule-rich;secretion-ready','Granule colors are design choices, not unstained biological colors. Do not identify all granular epithelial cells as Paneth cells.','GUT','Closest baseline: goblet cell has a mucus-filled apical cup; Paneth granules should not be drawn as that cup.')
a('A012','Type II pneumocyte with secretion anchors','Cells','Type II pneumocytes are comparatively compact alveolar epithelial cells that secrete surfactant.','Plan a compact cell cutaway with a nucleus, apical secretion positions and lateral junction anchors. Fit it as a discrete cell in an alveolar wall; expose an apical face toward airspace. Use library vesicles for secretion.','generic epithelial cell;secretory vesicle','resting;secretion-ready','The verified distinction is compact secretory cell versus thin type I cell. Detailed lamellar-body ultrastructure remains outside this specification.','LUNG','Closest baseline: generic epithelial cell; alveolar placement and secretion interfaces motivate this specialized cutaway.')

