p('P003','Intestinal endocrine-cell identity preset','Cells','Endocrine cells in intestinal crypts produce gastrointestinal hormones.','Reuse a generic epithelial cell with an endocrine identity label and an optional secretion annotation. Do not create one new silhouette for every hormone.','generic epithelial cell;secretory vesicle','unlabeled archetype;named hormone annotation','The source does not establish a unique silhouette for each endocrine subtype. Detailed polarity requires subtype-specific verification.','GUT','generic epithelial cell')
p('P004','Fenestrated endothelial-cell preset','Cells','Fenestrated capillary endothelium contains pores that support molecular exchange.','Reuse an endothelial cell, with a removable pore-pattern overlay away from the nucleus. Keep the basement membrane as another component.','endothelial cell;basement membrane','continuous;fenestrated overlay','Fenestrae and intercellular gaps are different features; do not make all fenestrated barriers equally permeable.','CAP','endothelial cell')
