p('P006','PD-1 identity preset','Immunology','PD-1 acts as an inhibitory receptor in T-cell signaling.','Reuse the single-pass immunoglobulin-like receptor. Put the binding anchor outside the membrane and the phosphatase-association annotation inside.','single-pass immunoglobulin-like receptor','unligated;ligated;phosphorylation overlay','Use a generic topology unless the precise domain structure is independently checked.','PD1','single-pass immunoglobulin-like receptor')
p('P007','PD-L1 identity preset','Immunology','PD-L1 participates as a PD-1 ligand.','Use a membrane-tethered ligand with a PD-L1 text label, keeping its extracellular binding anchor compatible with P006.','generic membrane-tethered ligand','available;antibody-occupied','A ligand label does not establish exact ectodomain geometry or glycosylation.','PD1','generic membrane-tethered ligand')
p('P008','Signaling kinase identity preset','Signaling','TCR and BCR pathways use named kinases such as LCK, ZAP-70 and SYK.','Reuse the enzyme archetype with independent name and phosphorylation overlays. Expose substrate and recruiter anchors; change labels rather than generate a new blob for each kinase.','generic enzyme','inactive annotation;active annotation;recruited','Activity annotations are context-dependent; color alone must not imply activation.','TCR;BCR','generic enzyme')
p('P009','Signaling phosphatase identity preset','Signaling','PD-1-associated phosphatases attenuate signaling by dephosphorylation.','Reuse a generic enzyme with SHP-1 or SHP-2 as a label and a catalytic relationship to a selected substrate.','generic enzyme','free;recruited;substrate-associated','A generic phosphatase icon does not specify all downstream targets or exclude alternative mechanisms.','PD1','generic enzyme')
p('P010','STAT/IRF transcription-factor identity preset','Signaling','STAT1, STAT2 and IRF9 participate in type I interferon signaling.','Reuse protein and DNA-bound transcription-factor archetypes with independent labels. Assemble a named complex only when the correct partners are selected.','generic globular protein;transcription factor bound to DNA','cytosolic;nuclear;DNA-associated','Do not confuse STAT1 homodimer with STAT1/STAT2/IRF9 ISGF3.','IFN','generic globular protein')
p('P011','Transferrin with iron occupancy preset','Proteins','Transferrin carries iron and releases it in an acidified endosomal setting.','Use one generic protein instance labeled transferrin with two removable iron-occupancy tokens. Tokens are native circles labeled Fe; they are not drug icons.','generic globular protein','apo;one-site schematic;two-site schematic','The protein outline is an identity schematic, not a verified two-lobe structural depiction.','FERR','generic globular protein')
p('P012','Phosphorylation annotation preset','Signaling','Phosphorylation marks receptor and adaptor states in the selected signaling pathways.','Attach removable P tokens to named domains or tails, with an optional phosphosite label. Preserve the base asset unchanged.','generic globular protein;transmembrane protein','unmodified;phosphorylated','A P token is an annotation. Site and stoichiometry require a cited specific event.','TCR;BCR;INS','generic globular protein')
p('P013','RNA lariat topology preset','Nucleic acids','Splicing generates an intron lariat through a branch-point linkage.','Reuse an RNA strand, arrange a loop with a tail and add a branch-point connector. Keep the loop closure distinguishable from ordinary backbone continuation.','RNA strand','intron attached to downstream exon;released lariat','The branch linkage is not an ordinary 3-prime to 5-prime backbone bond.','SPLICE','RNA strand')
p('P014','Ligand-responsive RNA folding preset','Nucleic acids','Riboswitch ligand binding stabilizes a regulatory RNA conformation.','Reuse an RNA strand and a labeled ligand token. Provide two editable strand arrangements and a marked ligand pocket without asserting a sequence.','RNA strand;small-molecule drug','unbound conformation;bound conformation','The small-molecule asset is a generic symbol relabeled as the chosen metabolite; binding can increase or decrease expression.','RIBO','RNA strand')
p('P015','C3b-opsonized particle preset','Immunology','Surface-associated C3b can promote recognition and phagocytosis of a target.','Reuse a bacterial or particle asset and distribute independently selectable protein tokens labeled C3b along its outside. Keep a clean no-opsonin state.','rod-shaped bacterium;generic globular protein','uncoated;C3b-coated','Token density is qualitative and does not establish complement deposition measurements.','C3','rod-shaped bacterium')
p('P016','Annexin V fluorescent probe preset','Assays','Annexin V binds phosphatidylserine in a calcium-dependent manner.','Reuse a protein archetype with an attached fluorophore marker and an Annexin V label. Provide a lipid-facing binding anchor and separate fluorescence annotation.','generic globular protein;fluorescent dye','free;PS-associated','Annexin positivity alone is not a definitive cell-death classification.','ANNEX','generic globular protein;fluorescent dye')
p('P017','DNA cohesive-end preset','Nucleic acids','Compatible DNA ends permit ligation during restriction cloning.','Reuse duplex and single-strand fragments. Preserve strand direction, show a short overhang and allow explicit complementary sequence labels.','linear DNA fragment;single-stranded DNA','5-prime overhang;3-prime overhang;blunt comparison','Do not imply that all restriction enzymes leave the same kind of overhang.','CLONE','linear DNA fragment')
