# Composite recipes: independently authored layouts, never flattened replacement artwork.
c('C001','TCR proximal signaling sequence','Immunology','TCR engagement couples CD3 phosphorylation to ZAP-70 recruitment and adaptor signaling.','Place a T-cell membrane opposite a peptide-presenting surface. Anchor TCR/CD3 in the T-cell membrane and peptide-MHC opposite it; put labeled LCK, ZAP-70 and LAT nodes on the cytosolic side. Connect engagement, phosphorylation and recruitment in numbered steps, retaining an unstimulated comparison.','T-cell receptor alpha-beta heterodimer;CD3 complex;peptide-MHC class I complex;plasma membrane segment;preset:P008;preset:P012','resting;engaged;proximal signaling','This is a proximal schematic; CD4/CD8 context and downstream branches must be selected explicitly.','TCR','roadmap:9')
c('C002','BCR recognition to second messengers','Immunology','BCR signaling connects antigen recognition to ITAM kinases and downstream second-messenger pathways.','Use a B-cell outline with one enlarged membrane inset. Place BCR outside-facing, CD79 labels on its signaling partners and SYK/BLNK/PLC-gamma2 inside. Branch a labeled PLC step into DAG at the membrane and IP3 toward an ER calcium-release annotation. Keep ion tokens and pathway arrows editable.','B lymphocyte;B-cell receptor;plasma membrane segment;smooth endoplasmic reticulum;preset:P008;preset:P012','unbound;antigen-engaged;second-messenger response','Antigen valency and calcium dynamics vary. Do not draw every BCR as a permanently crosslinked cluster.','BCR','roadmap:6')
c('C003','Complement initiation and three outcomes','Immunology','Complement initiation routes converge on C3 cleavage and have distinct effector outputs.','Build three labeled initiation lanes merging at a C3 cleavage node. Split the output into C3b surface decoration, soluble inflammatory-fragment labels and a terminal membrane-pore panel. Use existing complement complexes and a particle; do not draw all three outcomes as the same arrow or protein.','complement C1 complex;complement membrane attack complex;preset:P015;plasma membrane segment','initiation;amplification;effector outcomes','Select a consistent C2-fragment naming convention before naming a convertase; historical conventions differ.','C3','roadmap:13')
c('C004','Class I peptide-loading itinerary','Immunology','Class I peptide loading occurs in the ER before surface delivery through the secretory pathway.','Arrange cytosol, ER lumen, Golgi and surface as distinct compartments. Move peptide tokens into the ER, associate them with class I MHC and route the loaded complex through Golgi to membrane. Label the beta-2-microglobulin partner without inventing a new protein silhouette.','MHC class I;peptide-MHC class I complex;linear peptide;rough endoplasmic reticulum;Golgi apparatus;transport vesicle;plasma membrane segment','unloaded;ER-loaded;surface-presented','This is the conventional loading route, not a complete description of cross-presentation.','MHCI','roadmap:8')
c('C005','Class II invariant-chain and peptide exchange','Immunology','Endosomal antigen processing and peptide exchange produce surface class II peptide complexes.','Place incoming antigen in an endocytic lane and class II/invariant-chain in a secretory lane. Merge in an acidic compartment; use removable labels for invariant-chain processing and CLIP exchange. Deliver the loaded class II complex to the surface facing a CD4 T-cell receptor panel.','MHC class II;peptide-MHC class II complex;late endosome;lysosome;linear peptide;CD4 receptor;T-cell receptor alpha-beta heterodimer','invariant-chain associated;CLIP-bearing;peptide-loaded','The invariant chain and CLIP are different states; do not show extracellular antigen loading directly onto ER class II as the default route.','MHCII','roadmap:8')
c('C006','Modular full IgE schematic','Immunology','IgE combines antigen-binding arms with an Fc region structurally distinct from IgG Fc.','Attach two existing Fab instances to the planned IgE Fc module, preserving each arm as a linked component. Provide antigen-facing endpoints and an Fc receptor-facing endpoint. Label the result a schematic; do not claim a complete crystallographic pose.','antibody Fab fragment;new:A004','unbound;antigen-associated placeholder','The Fc deposition verifies Fc architecture, not a universal whole-antibody arm angle.','IGEF','', 'P1')
c('C007','Allergen-triggered mast-cell degranulation','Immunology','Aggregation of IgE-bound Fc epsilon receptors can trigger mast-cell mediator release.','Use a mast-cell cutaway with membrane receptor instances and modular IgE outside. A multivalent allergen token bridges receptor-associated IgE; inside, connect a SYK/PLC/calcium annotation to separate granules and exocytosis arrows. Provide sensitized and activated panels.','mast cell;single-pass immunoglobulin-like receptor;secretory vesicle;composite:C006;preset:P008','sensitized;crosslinked;degranulating','Receptor subunits are named schematic groups; do not equate unbound soluble IgE with receptor crosslinking.','IGE','roadmap:15')
c('C008','PD-1 inhibitory contact','Immunology','PD-1 ligation recruits phosphatases that attenuate T-cell signaling.','Place a T-cell membrane opposite a ligand-bearing membrane. Align PD-1 with PD-L1 across the gap, recruit a SHP-labeled enzyme inside the T cell and draw an inhibitory connector to a named proximal signaling node. Keep ligand occupancy and inhibition as separate annotations.','plasma membrane segment;preset:P006;preset:P007;preset:P009;T-cell receptor alpha-beta heterodimer','unligated;ligated;phosphatase recruited','Checkpoint engagement is not a binary guarantee of cell inactivity; a blockade panel would need a specific intervention source.','PD1','roadmap:17')
c('C009','Type I interferon receptor-to-nucleus response','Immunology','Type I interferon signaling produces the STAT1/STAT2/IRF9 complex ISGF3.','Place one IFN ligand above IFNAR1/2. Attach JAK1 and TYK2 labels inside, then show separate STAT1, STAT2 and IRF9 instances assembling into a named group. Route that group through a nuclear boundary to a DNA-response annotation.','small globular cytokine;preset:P005;preset:P008;preset:P010;nucleus;DNA double helix','ligand-free;receptor-active;ISGF3 nuclear','Do not substitute a STAT1 homodimer for ISGF3 or imply every interferon uses this receptor.','IFN')
c('C010','Canonical WNT on/off comparison','Signaling','Canonical WNT stabilizes beta-catenin and changes its transcriptional role.','Create matched WNT-absent and WNT-present panels using the same membrane, Frizzled and nucleus. In the absent panel group Axin/APC/CK1/GSK3 labels around beta-catenin and route turnover to proteasome. In the present panel annotate LRP5/6 with Frizzled and route stabilized beta-catenin to LEF/TCF at DNA.','Frizzled receptor;transmembrane protein;generic globular protein;generic enzyme;proteasome;nucleus;DNA double helix','WNT absent;canonical response','Noncanonical WNT pathways are outside this recipe; generic protein nodes are not verified domain structures.','WNT')
c('C011','Neighbor-dependent NOTCH cleavage','Signaling','A membrane ligand on a neighboring cell triggers NOTCH cleavage and nuclear NICD signaling.','Place two adjacent cell membranes with ligand and Notch facing across the intercellular space. Mark extracellular and intramembrane cleavage as separate steps; detach an NICD-labeled token on the receiving cell side and route it to an RBPJ/MAML-labeled nuclear group.','Notch receptor;generic membrane-tethered ligand;plasma membrane segment;generic globular protein;nucleus','neighbor contact;cleavage;NICD nuclear','Keep the ligand membrane-bound and avoid depicting NICD as the entire intact receptor entering the nucleus.','NOTCH')
c('C012','Insulin receptor activation and attenuation','Signaling','Insulin-receptor phosphorylation recruits signaling pathways; internalization participates in attenuation.','Use matched surface and internalized receptor groups. Bind a labeled insulin token to the receptor, add cytosolic phosphorylation labels and branch to IRS and SHC nodes. Route an internalization arrow into a separate endosomal receptor state; retain an attenuation label rather than erasing every downstream event.','receptor tyrosine kinase dimer;linear peptide;preset:P012;generic globular protein;early endosome','unbound;phosphorylated;internalized','The generic receptor is a schematic; insulin receptor preassembly must not be drawn as ligand-induced dimerization of free monomers.','INS','roadmap:31')
c('C013','Mitochondrial commitment to intrinsic apoptosis','Cell biology','BCL-2-family control links cellular stress to mitochondrial release of apoptotic factors.','Place stress inputs beside a mitochondrion. Add BAX/BAK and anti-apoptotic regulator labels at the outer membrane, then a release arrow to cytochrome-c and an existing apoptosome group. Continue to a named caspase annotation and an apoptotic cell state.','mitochondrion;generic globular protein;apoptosome;apoptotic cell','restrained;outer-membrane permeabilization;downstream response','Keep outer and inner mitochondrial membranes distinct. This omits other death pathways and does not assert a universal irreversible threshold.','APOP','roadmap:34')
c('C014','Cargo enclosure and autolysosome formation','Cell biology','Macroautophagy encloses cargo before fusion with the lysosomal system.','Use the existing autophagosome as the closed state; construct an open double-membrane cup from membrane components for the preceding state. Place a cargo group inside, seal the cup and connect the resulting vesicle to a lysosome/autolysosome endpoint. Maintain two membrane contours at enclosure.','lipid bilayer cross-section;autophagosome;lysosome;generic globular protein','open phagophore;sealed autophagosome;autolysosome','An autophagosome is not a single-membrane endosome. Cargo-receptor specificity requires a separate source.','AUTO','roadmap:63')
c('C015','Ferritin shell and iron-core loading','Structural biology','Ferritin stores iron inside a protein shell.','Reuse the planned shell in matched empty and loaded states. Place independent iron-core fill and Fe tokens inside its cavity, add a qualitative storage arrow and keep the cutaway aperture distinct from a biological pore.','new:A001','empty;partly illustrated core;loaded cutaway','Fill fraction is illustrative, not a calibrated iron concentration or an exact uptake mechanism.','FERR')
c('C016','Transferrin uptake and receptor recycling','Cell biology','Transferrin releases iron after receptor-mediated uptake into an acidified endosomal setting.','Arrange plasma membrane, endosome and a return lane. Bind iron-bearing transferrin to a receptor token, internalize the group, detach iron tokens under an acidification label, then return receptor and apo-transferrin to the surface for release.','preset:P011;transmembrane protein;plasma membrane segment;early endosome','surface-bound;acidic release;recycled','The receptor token is topology-neutral and must be labeled; no particular receptor structure or iron-export machinery is claimed.','FERR')
c('C017','Fibrinogen cleavage to editable fibrin network','Extracellular matrix','Thrombin cleavage enables fibrin assembly into fibers.','Start with a few linked fibrinogen instances and a thrombin-labeled enzyme. Use cleavage annotations followed by an assembly arrow to existing fibrin fibers. Build the final mesh from repeated fibers with explicit junctions, optionally placing platelets within the network as another layer.','new:A002;generic enzyme;fibrin fiber;platelet','soluble precursor;cleavage;network','A network illustration does not specify polymerization kinetics or crosslink chemistry.','FIB','blood clot with platelets and fibrin')
c('C018','Platelet activation and recruitment loop','Hematology','Platelet agonists amplify recruitment and aggregation after activation.','Lay out resting and activated platelets along a vessel-wall context. Release labeled ADP/ATP tokens from the activated group, route them to neighboring platelet receptors and close a positive-feedback arrow. Keep alpha-IIb/beta-3 labels attached to integrin instances in an aggregation inset.','platelet;endothelial monolayer;ADP;ATP;integrin alpha-beta heterodimer','resting;activated;recruiting','Do not present the feedback loop as the full coagulation cascade or assign unsupported clotting-factor complexes.','PLT','blood clot with platelets and fibrin')
c('C019','Membrane protein in a nanodisc','Structural biology','A scaffold belt stabilizes a small bilayer disc that can hold a membrane protein.','Arrange lipid instances into a bilayer patch, wrap its hydrophobic edge with the planned scaffold belt and insert an existing transmembrane protein through the patch. Provide top and tilted side views with individually selectable belt, lipids and protein.','new:A007;lipid bilayer cross-section;transmembrane protein','empty disc;protein-containing disc','Protein copy number, belt count and dimensions remain configurable; this is not a claim about a specific preparation.','NANO','', 'P1')
c('C020','Riboswitch ligand-dependent state comparison','Nucleic acids','Ligand binding can stabilize a regulatory RNA fold and alter gene expression.','Duplicate the same RNA preset into unbound and bound panels. Keep ligand identity and the expression-platform region labeled. Use an editable output badge reading increased or decreased expression only after the chosen riboswitch class is specified.','preset:P014;messenger RNA','unbound;ligand-bound','No universal ON direction is implied; a particular terminator or ribosome-binding-site mechanism needs additional verification.','RIBO')
c('C021','Telomerase repeat-extension cycle','Nucleic acids','Telomerase uses an internal RNA template to extend a telomeric DNA end.','Place the DNA 3-prime end against an RNA-containing protein group labeled telomerase. Align a short RNA template region with the extension site; show repeat addition and repositioning as separate arrows. Preserve DNA/RNA identities and strand-end labels throughout.','telomere;single-stranded DNA;RNA strand;generic globular protein;nucleotide','aligned;extended;repositioned','Sequence labels and repeat length must specify organism; the overview does not model complete telomere replication.','TELO','roadmap:55')
c('C022','Telomeric overhang versus quadruplex state','Nucleic acids','Guanine-rich telomeric DNA can form quadruplex structures.','Reuse one telomere context and replace only its exposed overhang state with the planned G-quadruplex module. Use a reversible state connector and retain strand endpoints. Keep optional shelterin labels outside the fold instead of embedding all telomere proteins in one icon.','telomere;single-stranded DNA;new:A008','extended overhang;quadruplex schematic','Do not portray quadruplex folding as obligatory at all chromosome ends.','TELO','roadmap:55')
c('C023','Spliceosomal branch formation and exon joining','Nucleic acids','Spliceosomal chemistry forms an intron lariat and joins the flanking exons.','Represent two exon blocks connected by an intron strand. Place the existing spliceosome around the junction and mark the branch point. Step one forms a loop linked to the downstream exon; step two joins exons and releases the lariat preset. Preserve exon colors between states.','spliceosome;RNA strand;messenger RNA;preset:P013','pre-mRNA;branched intermediate;joined exons and lariat','This depicts the major spliceosome pathway; branch linkage must not look like an ordinary backbone continuation.','SPLICE','roadmap:27')
c('C024','Four-way DNA junction conformation comparison','Nucleic acids','Four-way DNA junction geometry can vary with sequence and conditions.','Instantiate the same four-arm topology twice, once open for explanation and once stacked. Use consistent strand colors across the views, with labeled arm endpoints. Connect views using a conformation arrow, not a cleavage arrow.','new:A009;DNA double helix','open explanatory view;stacked view','The deposited structure supports a particular stacked geometry; an open depiction is a teaching layout, not a second measured structure.','HJ','roadmap:36')
c('C025','Restriction cloning with orientation check','Methods','Compatible ends enable ligation, while screening is needed to verify the resulting construct.','Arrange donor, cut insert and opened recipient plasmid in parallel lanes; match end labels before joining. Follow ligation with transformation and a separate verification checkpoint. Keep incorrect orientation as an optional clearly marked alternative, not a successful endpoint.','circular plasmid DNA;linear DNA fragment;preset:P017;generic enzyme;bacterial colony on agar;DNA electrophoresis gel with bands','donor and recipient;compatible ends;candidate clone;verified construct','Colony growth alone is not construct verification; this diagram is a conceptual workflow, not an operational protocol.','CLONE')
c('C026','Overlap-based Gibson assembly mechanism','Methods','Gibson assembly combines exonuclease, polymerase and ligase activities on overlapping fragments.','Place color-coded fragments with matched overlap labels. Show exposed complementary regions after end processing, annealing, gap filling and nick sealing as four distinct states. Retain the same fragment colors in the assembled product and show circularization only for a circular design.','linear DNA fragment;single-stranded DNA;generic enzyme;circular plasmid DNA','overlap design;annealed;filled;sealed','Overlaps are designed homology, not arbitrary restriction overhangs; no reaction conditions are specified.','GIBSON')
c('C027','Type IIS ordered assembly logic','Methods','Golden Gate assembly uses cleavage outside recognition sites to produce designed ligation ends.','Use several color-coded DNA modules with separate recognition-site and overhang labels. Draw cleavage outside each recognition site, then order fragments by compatible ends. Keep removed recognition regions visibly excluded from the intended joined product.','linear DNA fragment;preset:P017;generic enzyme;circular plasmid DNA','site-bearing modules;cut modules;ordered product','Directionality depends on the chosen overhang design; do not imply every arbitrary mixture self-orders.','GOLD')
c('C028','Single-cell ATAC partition and library workflow','Single-cell methods','The described single-cell ATAC workflow transposes nuclei before partitioning.','Start with nuclei and a transposition step outside droplets. Then partition with a barcoded bead, connect barcode incorporation to indexed library fragments and end with a sequencing/read-assignment panel. Label empty and multiplet partitions as possible states.','nucleus;transposase-DNA complex;single-cell droplet with barcoded bead;barcoded capture bead;indexed DNA library fragment;sequencing flow cell','bulk transposition;partitioning;barcoded library','One partition barcode does not guarantee one biological cell. The order is specific to the cited assay generation.','ATAC','roadmap:56')
c('C029','Joint RNA and antibody-tag measurement','Single-cell methods','Antibody oligonucleotide tags can be measured alongside gene expression in a single-cell workflow.','Place a surface-bound barcoded antibody on a cell, then put the cell and a capture bead in a partition. Split output into RNA-derived library and antibody-tag library while retaining a common cell-barcode label. Use distinct colors and labels for feature identity versus cell identity.','rounded suspension cell;preset:P018;single-cell droplet with barcoded bead;messenger RNA;indexed DNA library fragment','labeled cells;partition;two linked measurements','A tag count is assay evidence, not an exact molecule count or proof of target function.','FEATURE','roadmap:56')
c('C030','Captured guide identity linked to transcriptome','Single-cell methods','Captured CRISPR guide identities can be linked to single-cell gene-expression data.','Show a cell with a guide-RNA label, a partition and two output tracks: guide identity and transcriptome. Join tracks with the shared cell-barcode field. End with an association panel, leaving perturbation efficacy as a separate validation badge.','guide RNA;rounded suspension cell;single-cell droplet with barcoded bead;messenger RNA;barcoded oligonucleotide','guide-bearing cell;captured identity;linked readouts','Guide detection does not establish successful editing or prove that an observed expression change is causal.','FEATURE','roadmap:56')
c('C031','Sample multiplexing with distinct barcode roles','Single-cell methods','Sample tags add sample identity to single-cell measurements.','Give each input sample a distinct tag label, pool the cell groups and route them into partitions. At output show separate fields for sample tag, cell barcode and feature identity; include ambiguous-tag assignments as unresolved.','cell hashing antibody-tag complex;rounded suspension cell;single-cell droplet with barcoded bead;barcoded oligonucleotide','separate samples;pooled;assigned or ambiguous','Do not conflate a sample tag with a unique cell barcode or assume every cell has a clean sample assignment.','FEATURE','roadmap:56')
c('C032','Annexin and membrane-integrity interpretation panel','Assays','Annexin V reports accessible phosphatidylserine; membrane damage affects interpretation.','Build a membrane inset with PS labels and a calcium-dependent Annexin probe. Pair it with a membrane-impermeant-dye annotation and an editable two-axis schematic. Label quadrants by measured positivity first; annotate double positivity as compatible with late apoptotic or other dead cells.','plasma membrane segment;phospholipid;preset:P016;fluorescent dye;apoptotic cell;necrotic cell','Annexin negative or positive;integrity-dye negative or positive','Do not label every double-positive cell late apoptotic or treat Annexin alone as a definitive death assay.','ANNEX','roadmap:104')
c('C033','Intestinal crypt epithelial composition','Tissue biology','Intestinal crypts contain multiple epithelial cell types including Paneth and endocrine cells.','Use the crypt as a context frame. Place repeated epithelial instances along its wall, Paneth cells at the base and independently labeled endocrine and goblet cells among them. Keep the lumen unobstructed and cell identities selectable.','intestinal crypt;columnar epithelial cell;goblet cell;new:A011;preset:P003','overview;cell-type inset','This is a composition map, not a validated stem-cell lineage trajectory or a quantitative cell-frequency chart.','GUT','roadmap:88')
c('C034','Villus exchange routes and brush border','Tissue biology','Villi combine an absorptive epithelium with blood and lymphatic vessels.','Use a villus context and add an enlarged apical brush-border inset from enterocyte presets. Draw separate capillary and lacteal paths inside the villus, with labels rather than an undifferentiated vascular tube. Keep lumen-to-epithelium direction clear.','intestinal villus;preset:P002;goblet cell;capillary cross-section;lymphatic vessel','whole villus;surface inset','Nutrient-specific transporters and blood-versus-lymph routing need additional substrate-specific evidence.','GUT','roadmap:88')
c('C035','Alveolar air-blood diffusion barrier','Tissue biology','Thin alveolar epithelium and capillary endothelium form the gas-exchange interface.','Build an alveolar wall from flattened type I presets, basement-membrane components and endothelial cells. Place airspace on one side and erythrocytes in a capillary lumen on the other. Add independent O2 and CO2 arrows with opposing directions across the barrier.','alveolus;preset:P001;basement membrane;endothelial cell;erythrocyte','tissue view;barrier inset','Widths and distances are schematic; do not represent cell layers as equal-thickness slabs or claim a measured diffusion rate.','LUNG','roadmap:87')
c('C036','Type II cell surfactant secretion context','Tissue biology','Type II pneumocytes secrete surfactant toward the alveolar airspace.','Place the planned type II cell among type I cell presets. Orient secretion anchors toward the airspace; move separate vesicle instances toward that face and add a surface-film annotation. Keep the surfactant layer distinct from the basement membrane below the cells.','new:A012;preset:P001;secretory vesicle;alveolus','stored secretion;apical release;surface film','The film is a symbolic overlay; molecular surfactant composition and lamellar-body detail are not specified.','LUNG','roadmap:87')
c('C037','Capillary wall architecture comparison','Tissue biology','Continuous, fenestrated and sinusoidal capillary architectures differ.','Create three matched vessel cross-section panels with consistent lumen orientation. Reuse endothelial and basement-membrane components; add fenestrae as intracellular pore overlays and sinusoidal discontinuities as a separately labeled pattern. Use an optional external pericyte only in the appropriate contextual panel.','capillary cross-section;endothelial cell;preset:P004;basement membrane;new:A010','continuous;fenestrated;sinusoidal','Do not generalize pore sizes, basement-membrane continuity or permeability to every organ from the generic panels.','CAP','roadmap:86')
c('C038','Pericyte-endothelial spatial relationship','Tissue biology','Pericytes associate with the abluminal side of capillary endothelium.','Use a short endothelial tube or existing vessel context and place pericyte processes along its exterior. Add a cutaway showing lumen, endothelial layer and exterior cell contact. Keep pericyte and endothelium as different selectable cell groups.','small blood vessel;endothelial cell;new:A010;basement membrane','longitudinal view;cross-section inset','This establishes location, not a universal pericyte coverage fraction or molecular signaling mechanism.','CAP','roadmap:85')
c('C039','Outer-membrane porin diffusion and reduced access','Microbiology','Porins provide diffusion paths; reduced permeability can contribute to resistance.','Insert porin instances into the outer membrane of the Gram-negative envelope. Route a labeled compatible solute through the lumen into periplasm in one panel; reduce channel availability or show restricted passage in the comparison. Keep the inner membrane separate and do not add an ATP-consumption arrow.','Gram-negative cell-envelope cross-section;new:A005;small-molecule drug','permeable schematic;reduced-access schematic','Permeability effects depend on compound and porin. Reduced entry does not by itself prove clinical antibiotic resistance.','PORIN','roadmap:84')
c('C040','LPS position in a Gram-negative envelope','Microbiology','LPS combines lipid anchoring with carbohydrate regions at the bacterial surface.','Reuse the Gram-negative envelope frame and attach LPS lipid regions into the outer-facing membrane leaflet. Extend carbohydrate chains toward the extracellular side, leaving periplasm and inner membrane distinct. Use variable chain lengths as qualitative variants.','Gram-negative cell-envelope cross-section;new:A003','short carbohydrate schematic;extended carbohydrate schematic','Carbohydrate composition varies; do not call every generic chain a specific bacterial serotype.','LPS','roadmap:72')
c('C041','Aggrecan-collagen cartilage matrix organization','Extracellular matrix','Aggrecan and collagen contribute different structural features to cartilage matrix.','Place aggrecan brush instances between collagen fibrils around a chondrocyte context. Keep collagen, aggrecan cores and side chains as separate groups. Offer intact and reduced-aggrecan illustrative states with identical layout for comparison.','new:A006;collagen fibril;chondrocyte;extracellular matrix mesh','organized matrix;reduced-aggrecan comparison','Do not infer stiffness values, disease severity or a specific degradation enzyme from the schematic density.','AGG','roadmap:99')
c('C042','STING trafficking to interferon-response signaling','Immunology','STING signaling involves a localization change and TBK1/IRF3-dependent response.','Place a STING-labeled membrane protein at ER, add a trafficking arrow toward a Golgi/perinuclear state and connect TBK1 and IRF3 labels to a nuclear response annotation. Keep activation input as an explicitly unspecified upstream node.','smooth endoplasmic reticulum;Golgi apparatus;transmembrane protein;generic enzyme;generic globular protein;nucleus','ER-localized;trafficked;downstream response','This source mixes historical human and mouse evidence. A cGAS/cGAMP mechanism or species-specific residues require a newer targeted source.','STING')

